# Theming: Light/Dark Mode

This template ships with a basic, doc-site-aligned light/dark mode.

## Goals
- Mirror the look-and-feel of the FARM docs site
- Zero FOUC (no flash of wrong theme) on load
- Persisted theme choice (light/dark/system)
- Semantic Tailwind tokens instead of hard-coded grays

## References
- Live site: https://farm-rho-green.vercel.app/
- Reference images in `reference-images/`:
  - `title.png`, `landing.png`, `landinghigh.png`, `quickstart.png`, `ref.png`
- Tailwind and CSS are aligned with docs and already configured here:
  - `apps/web/tailwind.config.js.hbs`
  - `apps/web/src/index.css.hbs`

## How it works
- `index.html.hbs` contains a tiny inline script that reads the persisted theme from the app store key `{{projectName}}-app-store` and sets the `dark` class on `<html>` before CSS loads.
- `useAppStore` (Zustand) holds `theme: 'light' | 'dark' | 'system'` and persists it.
- `Layout` reacts to theme changes and toggles the `dark` class at runtime. It also shows a Theme Toggle button that cycles through light → dark → system.
- Components/pages were updated to use semantic colors: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.

## Files touched
- `apps/web/index.html.hbs`: no-FOUC theme script
- `apps/web/src/components/layout/Layout.tsx.hbs`: ThemeToggle and runtime `dark` class sync, semantic tokens in nav
- `apps/web/src/pages/Home.tsx.hbs`: semantic tokens
- `apps/web/src/pages/About.tsx.hbs`: semantic tokens
- `apps/web/src/components/ui/loading.tsx.hbs`: semantic tokens

## Using it
- Click the theme icon in the top-right of the nav to cycle modes.
- Default is `system`, following the OS preference.

## Notes
- Tailwind is set with `darkMode: 'class'` and color variables come from `index.css.hbs` using OKLCH values to match brand palette.
- The brand accent uses `bg-primary`/`text-primary` and `text-farm-green` for the primary green when needed.

## Future enhancements
- Add an accessible dropdown to explicitly choose Light/Dark/System.
- Animate the theme switch with subtle transitions.
